```dafny
// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Step-by-step math CSD with delimiter-sensitive modes. The strategy tracks
// whether generation is currently inside an arithmetic span (`insideConstrainedOut`)
// and, when it is, the exact constrained contents between `<<` and `>>`
// (`currentConstrainedOut`). Outside spans it generates freely, but as soon as
// it sees the opening delimiter token `"<<"` it switches to parser-constrained
// decoding so the arithmetic content stays parser-valid.
//
// Inside a constrained span, the strategy chooses between two verified actions
// based on local structure. If the parser says the span is complete, it closes
// the span immediately with `CloseConstrainedSpan`. Otherwise it uses
// `AdaptiveConstrainedStep` with the caller-supplied `validTokenGroups` to
// softly favor preferred arithmetic tokens when the parser's valid-next set is
// narrow, while still hard-masking to parser-valid continuations plus EOS.
// This tracked state ensures that the constrained suffix of `generated` always
// matches `currentConstrainedOut`, which is exactly what lets the parser govern
// the contents of each `<< ... >>` arithmetic derivation.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: In the unconstrained branch, if the sampled token is not
//   `"<<"` we remain outside the span, so the implication is vacuous; if it is
//   `"<<"` we set `currentConstrainedOut := []`, and `parser.IsValidPrefix([])`
//   holds by precondition. In the close branch, `CloseConstrainedSpan` returns
//   `insideConstrainedOut == false`, again making the implication vacuous. In
//   the adaptive constrained branch, `AdaptiveConstrainedStep` guarantees either
//   EOS or a token whose append preserves parser validity; on non-EOS we call
//   `AppendConstrainedToken`, whose precondition is exactly that validity fact.
// suffix: In the unconstrained branch, when we stay outside the span the suffix
//   invariant is vacuous; when we open a span on `"<<"`, we set
//   `currentConstrainedOut := []`, and the length-0 suffix of `generated` is
//   `[]`. In the close branch, `CloseConstrainedSpan` appends at most the close
//   delimiter and resets `currentConstrainedOut` to `[]`, so the implication is
//   vacuous afterward. In the adaptive constrained branch, the sampled non-EOS
//   token is appended to both `generated` and `currentConstrainedOut` via
//   `AppendConstrainedToken`, so the generated suffix continues to equal the
//   constrained prefix.
